## 2026-09-21 — device-deploy session: OOM-on-launch crash found + fixed (feat/capability-rollout-2026-09)
- First device deploy of the phases 6-9 build (mntm-012 test rig/API 87.1).
  It did not open: two of three launches rebooted the Flipper with the
  framework's "out of memory" screen.
- Root cause (SD breadcrumb instrumentation, reverted after): App state is ONE
  contiguous malloc of 20644 B taken at entry, where the largest free block
  measured 27640 B in a good heap state and dipped below the need in a worse
  one - a fragmentation failure, not total-free starvation (38880 B was free
  when the 20644 B allocation failed). The record queue was 8 KiB of that
  (32 slots x 256 B = 40%); phases 4-9 had grown the struct without a deploy.
- Fix: RECORD_QUEUE_CAPACITY 32 -> 8 (App 14500 B) + NULL-checked app-state
  allocation that logs/sounds and exits instead of letting the framework
  reboot the device. Runtime contiguous headroom after startup: 4176 -> 9912 B.
- Verified on device: 10/10 launch->exit cycles clean, entry heap stable
  across cycles (free ~38770, maxblk ~29200+). Receipt:
  .omo/evidence/oom-regression-2026-09-21.md. Gates: init.sh ALL PASS (24
  suites), _verify_api.py CLEAN, ufbt zero warnings.
- Lesson recorded in the receipt: phases 6-9 were host-verified only; this is
  exactly the class of defect the per-phase device gate exists to catch.

